<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish Feb unemployment fell to 259,500 - CSO.</title>
<headline>Irish Feb unemployment fell to 259,500 - CSO.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of people claiming unemployment benefit fell to a seasonally adjusted 259,500 in February from 262,400 in January, Central Statistics Office data said on Friday.</p>
<p>	     Unadjusted	 Adjusted</p>
<p>Latest	 264,310	   259,500</p>
<p>Previous     268,890	   262,400</p>
<p>Year-ago     286,770	   282,000</p>
<p>(No percentage of the total workforce was given)</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom +353 1 661 3377</p>
</text>
